# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same two in Vercel.
# Leave both unset and the app runs entirely in this browser — no auth, no network.
#
# Both come from the Supabase dashboard: Project Settings -> API Keys.
#
# The URL looks like https://<project-ref>.supabase.co, where the ref is
# exactly 20 lowercase characters. A short one means the copy dropped a
# character, and the app will say so on boot rather than failing obscurely.
#
# The key is whichever the dashboard offers: the new `sb_publishable_...` or
# the legacy `eyJ...` anon key. Both are meant to be public — row-level
# security is what protects the data. Never put a `sb_secret_...` or
# service_role key here; those bypass every policy.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
